From: oveRTOS <noreply@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] mps2-an500: end the heap with SSRAM2&3, not PSRAM

Patch 0001 links kernel RAM into SSRAM2&3 at 0x20000000. The idle stack
then lies above the 4 MB code SSRAM, so up_allocate_heap() takes the
"external region" branch and runs the heap on to PRIMARY_RAM_END, the end
of the 16 MB PSRAM: 0x2003c468-0x60fffff8, across unmapped space and the
peripherals, with its end node in the PSRAM the Linux personality uses
for the guest pool. Make SSRAM2&3 the primary RAM so the heap ends at
0x20400000.

diff --git a/arch/arm/src/mps/hardware/mps_memorymap.h b/arch/arm/src/mps/hardware/mps_memorymap.h
index 6bd9c83..04038b3 100644
--- a/arch/arm/src/mps/hardware/mps_memorymap.h
+++ b/arch/arm/src/mps/hardware/mps_memorymap.h
@@ -164,8 +164,12 @@
 #define MPS_PSRAM_START    0x60000000
 #define MPS_PSRAM_SIZE     0x01000000
 
-#define PRIMARY_RAM_START  MPS_PSRAM_START
-#define PRIMARY_RAM_SIZE   MPS_PSRAM_SIZE
+/* Kernel RAM is linked into SSRAM23 (see this board's flash.ld), and the heap
+ * must end with it rather than run on to the end of PSRAM.
+ */
+
+#define PRIMARY_RAM_START  MPS_SRAM2_START
+#define PRIMARY_RAM_SIZE   MPS_SRAM2_SIZE
 
 #if CONFIG_MM_REGIONS > 1
 #define REGION1_RAM_START  MPS_SRAM2_START
